{"name":"North Woods","hex":"#555a51","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"North Woods","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Laurentian Mixed Forest Province, a forested ecoregion in the United States and Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/North_Woods"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laurentian Mixed Forest Province","blocks":[{"text":"The Laurentian Mixed Forest Province, also known as the Northwoods, is a forested ecoregion in eastern Upper Midwest North America in the United States and Canada. Similar, though not necessarily identical regions, are identified by the United States Environmental Protection Agency as Northern Lakes and Forests and by the World Wildlife Fund, regions such as the Western Great Lakes forests and Eastern forest-boreal transition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/North_Woods.gif/330px-North_Woods.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurentian_Mixed_Forest_Province","wikidata":"Q2070727"},{"title":"North Woods (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"North Woods is a 2023 novel by American novelist Daniel Mason. The novel, Mason's sixth, is a work of historical fiction that tells the story of a single house in New England over the course of several centuries."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/North_Woods_US_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Woods_(novel)","wikidata":"Q123509612"},{"title":"North","blocks":[{"text":"North is one of the four compass points or cardinal directions. It is the opposite of south and is perpendicular to east and west. North is a noun, adjective, or adverb indicating direction or geography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Compass_Rose_English_North.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_North.svg.png?utm_source=en.wiki